# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a function call (OP_CALL) hits a safepoint at call-frame-push;
#         a non-top-level OP_RET hits a safepoint at frame-pop; both
#         decrement instruction_budget_remaining correctly.
#
# defer-to: T39
#
# Reason: verifying safepoint fires at OP_CALL requires host hooks to observe
# instruction_budget_remaining before and after a call within a single
# dispatch quantum.  A pure urbiscript test (function call that returns a
# value) would exercise the path but cannot assert the budget decrement.
# The chk runner is REPL-only; T39 adds ## host: hooks for this.
#
# Note: function call correctness (return value, frame push/pop) is already
# verified in tests/unit/test_dispatch_loop.c::dispatch_nested_call_and_ret
# which directly tests the C dispatch_loop_until_yield interface.  This
# fixture targets the safepoint budget-accounting aspect specifically.
#
# When T39 lands, implement this fixture by:
#   ## host: set URBI_STRAND_BUDGET_MAX=10; record budget_before_call
#   function f() { 42 }; f()
#   ## host: record budget_after_call; assert budget decreased by >= 2
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 42
